; Tick-count OHLC bars over a market feed.
;
; Producers publish raw prices on MARKET.<SYM> (e.g. MARKET.AAPL "182.34").
; Every 60 ticks per symbol, ohlc-bar emits four sub-subjects:
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.open   first price in the bar
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.high   max price seen
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.low    min price seen
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.close  60th price (the one that closed the bar)
;
; State is per (rule, subject), so each ticker builds its own bars. The
; in-progress bar is part of the snapshot, so a restart mid-bar resumes
; without losing the open / high / low collected so far.
(on "MARKET.*"
  (ohlc-bar 60 payload-float))

; Downstream alerting can sit on the closed-bar stream and stay clean of
; intra-bar noise. Example: alert if the bar's close jumps by >= 1.0
; from the prior bar's close on the same symbol.
(on "MARKET.*.bar.close"
  (when (>= (abs (delta payload-float)) 1.0)
    (publish (str-concat "alerts.market." (subject-token 1)) payload)))
